From: Warwick Allan <301310055+warwickallan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 14:58:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WO-OR-17: soft() preserves failure cause; no collapse of
 probe worlds

Keel's interrupted build completed and independently verified on handover.
soft() keeps the cause beside a null value so MEASURED ABSENCE and PROBE
FAILURE no longer render identically (TQA-001 cwd, TQA-002 symbolic-ref).
Also: unborn-branch uses measured symbolic-ref; deliverables sweep labels
symlink provenance; stdin read failure is not empty stdin.

Completion fix (Grok handover): branch render must not say DETACHED when
the probe failed, and exit-128 vs ENOENT must render as distinct lines.

Suite: 50/50 reorient; 268/268 all-eight in worktree.
